# =====================================
# SOURCE: ir_build_work/Flipper-IRDB/TVs/Sharp/Sharp_13VT-L100.ir
# =====================================
Filetype: IR signals file
Version: 1
#
# After digging through endless 2004 remote forums and trying every IRDB on the web, I ended up using bruteforce to make the important part of this file: the menu navigation buttons. Since it is a TV/VHS combo, the TV functions use sharp protocol device type 1 while the VHS side uses device type 3. All the files available online did not have the data to enter the menu which was my main reason for needing the remote as the on TV buttons don't work. The menu uses the "-" "+" buttons to navigate which are set as VHS device type 3 for some god unknown reason. This file emulates the Sharp G11330SA remote which should work with the following models: 13VT-CJ10, 13VT-CK10, 13VT-CL10, 13VT-CN10, 13VT-CR10, 13VT-J100, 13VT-K100, 13VT-L100, 13VT-N100, 13VT-R100, 20VT-J100, 25VS-J250, 25VT-CJ10, 25VT-CK10, 25VT-J100, 25VT-K100, VD-2568. This file is missing a lot of the VHS buttons but has what you need to get in the menu and change the settings.
#
name: Power
type: raw
frequency: 38000
duty_cycle: 0.330000
data: 264 1848 264 792 264 792 264 792 264 792 264 792 264 1848 264 1848 264 792 264 1848 264 792 264 792 264 792 264 1848 264 792 264 43560 264 1848 264 792 264 792 264 792 264 792 264 1848 264 792 264 792 264 1848 264 792 264 1848 264 1848 264 1848 264 792 264 1848 264 43560
